post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
==> Thyra is installed as /usr/bin/thyra. It needs a Herdr server.
==> Run it as a user service:
      systemctl --user enable --now thyra.service
    It listens on 127.0.0.1:8787. Settings go in ~/.config/thyra/thyra.env
    (mode 0600); see /usr/share/doc/thyra/thyra.env.example.
    `thyra user add <name> --admin` prints a passkey enrollment link.
==> Shell integration for Herdr panes (per user, edits your rc files):
      thyra shell-integration install --shell all
      thyra shell-integration status
==> `thyra service install` writes its own unit to ~/.config/systemd/user,
    which shadows the packaged one; use one or the other.
==> pacman manages updates; the in-app updater is disabled in the packaged unit.
MSG
}
